  "text": "Let's proceed with the steps outlined in the hint:\n\n1. Find ∠BAC using the Angle Bisector Theorem.\n2. Use the result to find the relationships between the angles.\n3. Finally, find the ratio of the measure of ∠ABD to the measure of ∠ABC.\n\n### Step 1: Find ∠BAC using the Angle Bisector Theorem.\n\nGiven: \\( \\angle BAC \\) is trisected by \\( AE \\) and \\( AF \\).\n\nBy the Angle Bisector Theorem, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{DB}{DC} = \\frac{AB}{AC}\n\\]\nThus:\n\\[\n\\frac{AB}{AC} = \\frac{DB}{DC}\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Using the Trisected Angles.\n\nGiven \\( \\angle BAC = 3x \\), then:\n\\[\n\\angle EAF = \\frac{3x}{3} = x\n\\]\n\nSince \\( AD \\) bisects \\( \\angle EAF \\):\n\\[\n\\angle BAF = \\angle FAD = \\frac{x}{2}\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\\[\n\\angle BAC = \\angle BAF + \\angle EAF = \\angle BAF + x = x + x = 2x\n\\]\nThus \\( \\angle BAC = 3x \\).\n\n### Step 3: Using \\( PDFGBE \\).\n\nRemember:\n\\[\n\\frac{DB^2}{DC^2} = \\frac{AB^2}{AC^2}\n\\]\nThus:\n\\[\n\\frac{AB}{AC} = \\frac{BD}{DC}\n\\]\n\nBy applying the Angle Bisector Theorem again:\n\\[\n\\frac{BD}{DC} = \\frac{AB}{AC}\n\\]\n\nAlso,\n\\[\n\\angle ABC = \\frac{2AB}{BC}\n\\]\n\nCombination clearly:\n\\[\n\\frac{AB}{BC} = \\frac{BD}{DC} = \\frac{AB}{AC}\n\\]\nThus:\n\\[\n\\frac{BD}{DC} = 1\n\\]\nThen:\n\\[\n\\angle ABD = 90^\\circ - \\angle DBC = 90^\\circ - \\angle ABC = 90^\\circ - \\frac{2AB}{AC}\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\\[\n\\frac{BD}{DC} = 1 \\implies \\angle ABC = \\frac{2AB}{AC}\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\angle ABD}{\\angle ABC} = \\frac{60^\\circ}{90^\\circ} = \\frac{2}{3}\n\\]\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{\\frac{2}{3}}\\)",
